WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:08.500
Every safety consulting firm runs the same ten steps, from winning the work to knowing what it earned. Here's one system that runs all of them.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:20.200
Win work. Your pipeline scores companies in your territory on public safety signals, like OSHA inspections. And proposals are built from your own services and rates.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:30.050
Onboard the client. A signed proposal becomes a contract: who brought it in, who services it, and who to call on the client side.

00:00:31.017 --> 00:00:40.417
Staff it. Every credential and its expiry in one place, so you can see who's qualified for the job, and who's actually free.

00:00:41.383 --> 00:00:50.533
Deliver it. Observations come in from the field with photos, a drafted description, and the OSHA standard, then roll up into reports on your own forms.

00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:58.683
Support delivery. Your toolbox talks, sign-in sheets, and courses sit right alongside the work.

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:07.450
Capture the work. Timesheets fill in from the schedule. Your consultant fixes what changed, signs, and collects the client signature.

00:01:08.417 --> 00:01:13.667
Bill it. Every contract shows what's been invoiced, and what's left to bill.

00:01:14.617 --> 00:01:23.467
Prove it. Corrective actions go to whoever owns the fix, by text, with a completion link. No login needed. And the closeout stays on the record.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:30.867
Show the client. Findings by client and by site, so every visit starts with what to look for.

00:01:31.817 --> 00:01:38.567
Run the business. What's under contract, what's been delivered, and what's left, across every client.

00:01:39.517 --> 00:01:44.967
Tell us which step costs your team the most time. That's the one we build around first.
